{"id": "tea:vedantaparibhasa:ch.1", "source": "src:vedantaparibhasa", "location": {"ref": "ch.1"}, "original": {"text": "anadhigatābādhitārthaviṣayakajñānatvaṃ pramātvam", "script": "IAST", "edition": "vulgate wording recalled from memory (verify against an edition)", "licence": "public domain (pre-modern text)"}, "paraphrase": "Valid cognition (pramā) is cognition of an object not already known and not contradicted; the means of knowledge are six — perception, inference, comparison, verbal testimony, presumption and non-cognition.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language", "consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:prama", "trm:pramana", "trm:arthapatti", "trm:anupalabdhi", "trm:upamana"], "concepts": ["cpt:pramana"], "disputes": ["dsp:number-of-pramanas"], "notes": "Original of the definition moderate-high confidence.", "teachers": ["tch:dharmaraja-adhvarindra"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vedantaparibhasa:ch.1/2", "source": "src:vedantaparibhasa", "location": {"ref": "ch.1"}, "paraphrase": "In perception the inner organ goes out through the sense to the object and takes its form (a vṛtti); then the consciousness delimited by the inner organ (the knower), by the vṛtti (the means) and by the object become one, and the object is perceived.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:vrtti", "trm:antahkarana", "trm:pratyaksa"], "concepts": ["cpt:perception-advaita"], "teachers": ["tch:dharmaraja-adhvarindra"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vedantaparibhasa:ch.4", "source": "src:vedantaparibhasa", "location": {"ref": "ch.4"}, "paraphrase": "Verbal testimony gives knowledge through expectancy, compatibility, proximity and intended purport; the Veda is not composed by a person but reproduced by Īśvara at each creation in the same order as before.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:sabda-pramana"], "disputes": ["dsp:status-of-veda"], "teachers": ["tch:dharmaraja-adhvarindra"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vedantaparibhasa:ch.7", "source": "src:vedantaparibhasa", "location": {"ref": "ch.7"}, "paraphrase": "Brahman has a defining mark of its own nature (svarūpa-lakṣaṇa: existence, consciousness, bliss) and an incidental mark (taṭastha-lakṣaṇa: being the cause of the world's origin, sustenance and dissolution), as a house is pointed out by the crow sitting on it.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "terms": ["trm:svarupa-laksana", "trm:tatastha-laksana"], "concepts": ["cpt:tatastha-svarupa-laksana"], "teachers": ["tch:dharmaraja-adhvarindra"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vedantaparibhasa:ch.7/2", "source": "src:vedantaparibhasa", "location": {"ref": "ch.7"}, "paraphrase": "Dissolution (pralaya) is fourfold: daily (deep sleep), occasional (at the end of Brahmā's day), elemental (of all effects into prakṛti at the end of Brahmā's life) and final (ātyantika, liberation through knowledge).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:pralaya"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-pralayas"], "teachers": ["tch:dharmaraja-adhvarindra"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vedantaparibhasa:ch.8", "source": "src:vedantaparibhasa", "location": {"ref": "ch.8"}, "paraphrase": "Liberation is the attainment of bliss and the removal of sorrow, which is Brahman itself; its means is the knowledge of Brahman, arising from hearing and the rest in one endowed with the four means; worship of the qualified Brahman leads to the Brahma-world and gradual liberation.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:liberation-advaita", "cpt:krama-mukti"], "paths": ["pth:advaita-sadhana"], "teachers": ["tch:dharmaraja-adhvarindra"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
